    <region left="18" top="0" width="760" height="26" color="#000000" fontSize="12">
      <text lang="eng" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="10">
        <content>
          <p style="font-size: 12px; font-weight: bold;">Grant Bellon</p>
        </content>
      </text>
    </region>
    <region left="18" top="38" width="760" height="26" color="#000000" fontSize="12">
      <text lang="eng" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="10">
        <content>
          <p style="font-size: 12px; font-weight: bold;">Lab [8]</p>
        </content>
      </text>
    </region>
    <region left="18" top="76" width="760" height="26" color="#000000" fontSize="12">
      <text lang="eng" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="10">
        <content>
          <p style="font-size: 12px; font-weight: bold;">Pump Curve and Efficiency Measurement</p>
        </content>
      </text>
    </region>
    <region left="18" top="124" width="760" height="26" color="#000000" fontSize="12">
      <text lang="eng" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="10">
        <content>
          <p style="font-size: 12px; font-weight: bold;">Introduction</p>
        </content>
      </text>
    </region>
    <region left="18" top="158" width="760" height="129" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
      <text lang="eng" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="10">
        <content>
          <p>The objective of this experiment was to measure the pump curves and efficiencies of two centrifugal pumps. A magnetically-driven pump was run through six vertical pipes of increasing height, and its discharge pressure, flowrate, and electrical power draw were recorded so the head at the pump discharge and at each pipe zenith could be compared. A transparent centrifugal pump testbench was run at full speed while its discharge valve was closed in steps from fully open to fully closed, recording the intake and discharge pressures and flowrate. The heads and efficiencies of both pumps were calculated, their uncertainties were propagated with the Kline-McClintock method, and the pump curves were overlaid on the Lab 6 system curve to find the operating points.</p>
        </content>
      </text>
    </region>
    <region left="18" top="303" width="760" height="26" color="#000000" fontSize="12">
      <text lang="eng" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="10">
        <content>
          <p style="font-size: 12px; font-weight: bold;">Given Data</p>
        </content>
      </text>
    </region>
